  <ym-title|Weighted frame and penalty \V draft source
  correspondence><label|weighted-frame-and-penalty--draft-source-correspondence>

  Source revision <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Output
  <verbatim|weighted-frame-penalty.tex> SHA256
  <verbatim|48da6807f04022a9559faba84cd05ba2dc08614efd32a53284fcf3ac6f594b29>.

  Inspected, namespace YM.Stationary:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/FrameEst/Averages.lean>: Hearing
    exact charge0/sup,1/L2,2/L1; Tested/Gallop positive jets;
    tested_compartment/tested_lite; convoyed length\<times\>inch bound;
    singer_patch via endpoint coordinate swap and translated injective reads,
    singer_leg/axes.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/FrameEst/Center.lean>:
    lottery_residue, salon_vote/stamp; vaulted/cap_thaw qualitative
    smoothness; chorus_eq, chorus_normal, chorus_compute exact
    weighted-center elimination; bass_cost and pre_choir derivative
    induction. Crucially D ringTone(1)=0 prevents same-order circularity.
    Weighted smoothing is not uniform on patch.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/FrameEst/Stencils.lean>:
    Sung.marks/stepUp/lower and crossing_stamp, agora_fare, airplay_funds,
    StaffP, slot1/piano_fare, canopy_sits, books_paid/cashBook. Finite fixed
    composition costs remain independent of L and incoming path budget. Fine
    jets preserve inch because every chain term has \<gtr\>=1 factors.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Block/Packing.lean>: Veil,
    mural_obey/inj/ports, mode_voice, carried_shine, shiny_steps. Padding
    costs fixed J only; complex real/imaginary stencil direction bounds
    checked.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Shape/Shim.lean>: ratePocket,
    seen_affect; coarse scalar ordinary norm and fine weighted Fourier norm.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Films/Site.lean>: rear_price,
    color_flick, flick_plank, lower_voice.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Spectral/Slabs.lean>: hill,
    hill_inch/tilt, plankTile, contour/altarTile;
    <verbatim|Spectral/Folding.lean>: rate_alias, plank_cap/back, cruise.
  </itemize-minus>

  Parent proof preserves the exact main induction and normalization
  identities; generic finite composition polynomials replace
  implementation-specific numeric names. Exact numerical minimal constants
  not claimed, only finite constants with the same quantifier order. Scalar
  norm is L2 (no unproved Sobolev strengthening). Fourier weights depend on
  real part of momentum and need not be holomorphic; no such claim made.

  Canonical reuse/literature: shared background notes inspected; existing
  qualitative frame/predictor construction reused. Elementary finite Hölder,
  product and partition chain rules proved or explained directly; no new
  external result invoked. Source declaration names are kept out of
  manuscript.

  Remaining supplier: quantitative smooth bridge Cruise. This unit closes
  weighted internal-leg and real block-penalty supplier conditional on the
  already constructed qualitative minimizer/predictor, group nearest-point
  properties, actual patch/kernels and Cruise. No global completion claim.

  Checks run: targeted rg/sed reads, SHA256. No fresh Lean build or axiom
  replay; source unchanged. Independent review pending.

  Independent bounded draft review passed at
  6c2d0c44cf05932f947d98731cec92ce755d6559b34f6b255248efbe6e8570d6
  (2026-11-12 05:23 UTC). Static inverse and selected linear-data units now
  supply each other\<#2019\>s explicit interfaces; full determinant-jet and
  finite-volume recording estimates remain separate obligations. No fresh
  Lean build.

